      "version": "2.0",
      "params": [],
      "data": {
        "filepath": "",
        "lang": "None",
        "width": 34,
        "etext": "MODULAR-SYNTH / ORIGINALS 004\nSTEREO ECHO SHOWCASE\n\nPlay HOST MIDI notes. Morph VCO is pitch-driven;\nADSR opens a conservative VCA before the filter.\n\nSTATE FILTER parallel low-pass and high-pass\noutputs feed STEREO ECHO left and right inputs.\nThis creates two distinct channels, so ECHO\nPING-PONG crossfeed makes an audible difference.\n\nECHO: 360 ms, 42% feedback, 52% wet, 80%\ncrossfeed. Stereo outputs go to host L/R.\nHost and VCA gain are reduced for headroom.\n\nThe delay uses milliseconds, NOT transport BPM.\nStereoEcho reserves about 23.44 MiB per instance.\nNo external audio samples or downloads needed.\n"
      },
      "pos": [
        80,
        0
      ]
    }
